---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Invite someone | Search OC"
	description="Three texts you can actually send, and what to say when they ask something you can't answer."
	canonical="/invite"
	ogImage="/og/invite.png"
	ogDescription="Three texts you can actually send, and what to say when they ask something you can't answer."
/>

<!-- Section 1: Hero -->
<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-10">
	<div class="max-w-3xl">
		<div class="uppercase tracking-[3px] text-xs font-sans text-[#2A6AA3] mb-3">FOR THE PERSON DOING THE INVITING</div>
		<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tighter">You have someone in mind. Here's how to ask.</h1>
		<p class="mt-4 text-xl text-[#243B48]">
			You already know who. You just don't know how to bring it up without it getting weird. That's what this page is for.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- Section 2: The ask is smaller than you think -->
<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 section border-t border-[#E5E7EB] bg-white">
	<div class="max-w-3xl">
		<h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The ask is smaller than you think</h2>
		<p class="mt-6 text-[#243B48]">
			You are not inviting anyone to church. You are inviting them to one table, for one hour, to talk about one honest question. Eight to twelve people, food, no sermon, no follow-up unless they ask for it.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 text-[#243B48]">
			They can come once and never come back, and nothing about your friendship changes. That is the whole deal. It is small on purpose.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4">
			<a href="/open-forums" class="text-[#2A6AA3] font-medium hover:underline">See exactly what a night looks like →</a>
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- Section 3: Three texts you can actually send -->
<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 section border-t border-[#E5E7EB]">
	<div class="max-w-3xl">
		<h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Three texts you can actually send</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 text-[#243B48]">
			Steal these. Change the words so they sound like you, then send it today while you still mean it.
		</p>

		<div class="mt-8 space-y-6">
			<!-- Card 1 -->
			<div class="card">
				<div class="text-sm font-sans font-semibold text-[#2A6AA3] uppercase tracking-[1.5px] mb-3">A close friend</div>
				<div class="border border-[#E5E7EB] rounded-xl p-5 bg-white">
					<p class="text-[#1A1A1A]">Random one for you. I go to this thing where eight or so people sit around a table over dinner and argue about God for an hour. Nobody preaches, nobody is selling anything. Honestly I just think you'd have things to say. Want to come with me?</p>
				</div>
				<button class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-[#2A6AA3] hover:underline copy-btn" data-target="text-1">Copy</button>
			</div>

			<!-- Card 2 -->
			<div class="card">
				<div class="text-sm font-sans font-semibold text-[#2A6AA3] uppercase tracking-[1.5px] mb-3">Someone you work with</div>
				<div class="border border-[#E5E7EB] rounded-xl p-5 bg-white">
					<p class="text-[#1A1A1A]">This is a little out of left field. There's a group I'm part of that gets a handful of people around a table over dinner and takes on one big question, like whether suffering makes God impossible. It's an hour, it's not a church thing, and you can disagree with everyone in the room. I thought of you. Any interest?</p>
				</div>
				<button class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-[#2A6AA3] hover:underline copy-btn" data-target="text-2">Copy</button>
			</div>

			<!-- Card 3 -->
			<div class="card">
				<div class="text-sm font-sans font-semibold text-[#2A6AA3] uppercase tracking-[1.5px] mb-3">Someone church has burned</div>
				<div class="border border-[#E5E7EB] rounded-xl p-5 bg-white">
					<p class="text-[#1A1A1A]">I want to run something by you, and it is completely fine to say no. There's a table I go to where people ask the questions about God that churches usually dodge. No worship, no sermon, no one is going to corner you at the end. The people who have been burned are usually the ones who make the night worth it. If you ever want to come, I'll sit next to you.</p>
				</div>
				<button class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-[#2A6AA3] hover:underline copy-btn" data-target="text-3">Copy</button>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- Section 4: What if they ask something I can't answer -->
<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 section border-t border-[#E5E7EB] bg-white">
	<div class="max-w-3xl">
		<h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">"What if they ask me something I can't answer?"</h2>
		<p class="mt-6 text-[#243B48]">
			You say: "I don't know. Come ask it out loud."
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 text-[#243B48]">
			That's it. That is the entire thing you have to be able to do.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 text-[#243B48]">
			You are not the expert and you were never supposed to be. You are the door. The table is where the question gets handled, and a question you can't answer is the best possible reason for them to show up.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 text-[#243B48]">
			The fastest way to lose someone is to bluff. "I don't know" is the most credible sentence you own. Use it.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- Section 5: Two things to hold onto -->
<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 section border-t border-[#E5E7EB]">
	<div class="max-w-3xl">
		<h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Two things to hold onto</h2>

		<div class="mt-8 space-y-8">
			<div>
				<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#1A1A1A]">God is responsible for the results.</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-[#243B48]">
					Your job is the invitation. Whether they come, what they think, what happens in them after, none of that is yours to carry. Show up, prepare, use what you've been given. Let go of the rest.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#1A1A1A]">A spiritual journey is a process.</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-[#243B48]">
					Nobody arrives in one conversation. One honest hour at a table is a real step, even if it is the only one you ever see. You are probably not the first person in this story and you will not be the last.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- Section 6: If they say no -->
<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 section border-t border-[#E5E7EB] bg-white">
	<div class="max-w-3xl">
		<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#1A1A1A]">If they say no</h3>
		<p class="mt-4 text-[#243B48]">
			Then you know where they are, which is more than you knew yesterday. You asked once, gently, and you didn't make it strange. Ask again next year. That is a fine outcome.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- Section 7: CTA -->
<section id="cta" class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 section border-t border-[#E5E7EB]">
	<div class="max-w-xl">
		<h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">You'll want to know the date</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 text-[#243B48]">
			Hard to invite anyone to a night that doesn't have a date yet. Leave your email and you'll know the moment the next table is set, early enough to ask before it fills.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-3 text-[#243B48]">
			If you already know who you're bringing, put their first name in. I'll watch for them and sit them somewhere good.
		</p>

		<form
			id="invite-form"
			class="mt-6 space-y-4"
			method="POST"
			action="/api/invite"
		>
			<div>
				<label for="email" class="block text-sm font-medium text-[#243B48] mb-1">Your email</label>
				<input
					type="email"
					id="email"
					name="email"
					required
					class="w-full rounded-lg border border-[#E5E7EB] bg-white px-4 py-3 text-[#1A1A1A] focus:border-[#EA7824] focus:outline-none"
					autocomplete="email"
				/>
			</div>
			<div>
				<label for="guestName" class="block text-sm font-medium text-[#243B48] mb-1">Who you're bringing (optional, first name is plenty)</label>
				<input
					type="text"
					id="guestName"
					name="guestName"
					class="w-full rounded-lg border border-[#E5E7EB] bg-white px-4 py-3 text-[#1A1A1A] focus:border-[#EA7824] focus:outline-none"
					autocomplete="off"
				/>
			</div>
			<button type="submit" id="submit-btn" class="btn-cta w-full min-h-11 inline-flex items-center justify-center">
				Keep me in the loop
			</button>
			<p class="text-xs text-[#3F3F46]">Two things show up in your inbox. The date of the next table, and Having Killer Conversations, a short note every other week for Christians who want to talk about their faith without being weird about it. Nothing else, and you can leave any time.</p>
		</form>

		<div id="form-success" class="hidden mt-6 rounded-xl border border-[#E5E7EB] bg-white p-6 text-[#243B48]">
			<p class="font-medium text-[#1A1A1A]">You're in. I'll email you the second the next table has a date.</p>
		</div>

		<div id="form-error" class="hidden mt-4 text-sm text-red-600">
			That didn't go through, which is on us, not you. Try again in a minute.
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<script is:inline>
	// Copy button handling for section 3
	document.querySelectorAll('.copy-btn').forEach((btn) => {
		btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
			const targetId = btn.getAttribute('data-target');
			const textMap = {
				'text-1': 'Random one for you. I go to this thing where eight or so people sit around a table over dinner and argue about God for an hour. Nobody preaches, nobody is selling anything. Honestly I just think you\'d have things to say. Want to come with me?',
				'text-2': "This is a little out of left field. There's a group I'm part of that gets a handful of people around a table over dinner and takes on one big question, like whether suffering makes God impossible. It's an hour, it's not a church thing, and you can disagree with everyone in the room. I thought of you. Any interest?",
				'text-3': 'I want to run something by you, and it is completely fine to say no. There\'s a table I go to where people ask the questions about God that churches usually dodge. No worship, no sermon, no one is going to corner you at the end. The people who have been burned are usually the ones who make the night worth it. If you ever want to come, I\'ll sit next to you.'
			};
			const text = textMap[targetId];
			if (!text) return;

			try {
				await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
				btn.textContent = 'Copied';
				btn.disabled = true;
				setTimeout(() => {
					btn.textContent = 'Copy';
					btn.disabled = false;
				}, 2000);
			} catch {
				// Clipboard write failed; text remains selectable in the block
			}
		});
	});

	// CTA form handling with progressive enhancement
	const form = document.getElementById('invite-form');
	const success = document.getElementById('form-success');
	const errorBox = document.getElementById('form-error');
	const submitBtn = document.getElementById('submit-btn');

	if (form && success && errorBox && submitBtn) {
		form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
			e.preventDefault();

			if (success) success.classList.add('hidden');
			if (errorBox) errorBox.classList.add('hidden');

			const formData = new FormData(form);
			const email = (formData.get('email') || '').toString().trim();

			if (!email || !email.includes('@')) {
				if (errorBox) {
					errorBox.textContent = 'Please enter a valid email.';
					errorBox.classList.remove('hidden');
				}
				return;
			}

			submitBtn.disabled = true;
			submitBtn.textContent = 'Sending...';

			try {
				const res = await fetch('/api/invite', {
					method: 'POST',
					headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
					body: JSON.stringify({
						email: email,
						guestName: (formData.get('guestName') || '').toString().trim()
					})
				});

				if (res.ok) {
					form.classList.add('hidden');
					if (success) success.classList.remove('hidden');
				} else {
					throw new Error('Submission failed');
				}
			} catch {
				if (errorBox) {
					errorBox.textContent = 'That didn\'t go through, which is on us, not you. Try again in a minute.';
					errorBox.classList.remove('hidden');
				}
			} finally {
				submitBtn.disabled = false;
				submitBtn.textContent = 'Keep me in the loop';
			}
		});
	}
</script>

<style>
	.card {
		border: 1px solid #E5E7EB;
		border-radius: 16px;
		padding: 1.5rem;
		background: white;
	}

	.btn-cta {
		background-color: #EA7824;
		color: white;
		padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
		border-radius: 12px;
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		transition: all 0.2s ease;
	}

	.btn-cta:hover {
		background-color: #d66a1a;
		transform: translateY(-1px);
	}

	.btn-cta:focus-visible {
		outline: 2px solid #EA7824;
		outline-offset: 2px;
	}

	.btn-cta:disabled {
		opacity: 0.6;
		cursor: not-allowed;
	}
</style>
